Subject: [PATCH 1/4] [QUICUI-PATCH] Add AOT Code Push support to Flutter
 Engine

This commit adds QuicUI Code Push functionality to the Flutter Engine.
This patch can be applied to newer Flutter SDK versions via cherry-pick or rebase.

Cherry-pick instructions:
  git cherry-pick <this-commit-hash>

Files modified:
- engine/src/flutter/shell/common/codepush_loader.h (new)
- engine/src/flutter/shell/common/codepush_loader.cc (new)
- engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/android/io/flutter/embedding/engine/loader/QuicUICodePushLoader.java (new)
- engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/android/io/flutter/embedding/engine/loader/FlutterLoader.java (modified)

What this adds:
1. AOT snapshot patching system for hot updates
2. Platform channel bridge: dev.quicui.code_push
3. Patch validation with SHA256 hash checking
4. Auto-fallback to original APK on corruption
5. Patch storage in code cache directory

How it works:
- Dart client downloads patch via HTTP
- Platform channel transfers patch to native
- QuicUICodePushLoader copies to /data/data/<pkg>/code_cache/quicui_patches/
- On app restart, FlutterLoader checks for patch
- Engine loads patched libapp.so instead of APK snapshot
- 3-layer security: hash verification at Dart, native, and engine levels

Platform Channel Methods:
- installPatch(patchPath, version, hash, architecture, signature)
- hasPatch() -> bool
- getInstalledPatchVersion() -> string
- clearPatch() -> bool
- getArchitecture() -> string
- restartApp()

Patch location: /data/data/<pkg>/code_cache/quicui_patches/libapp_patched_<arch>.so
Metadata: patch_metadata.json

Compatible with: Flutter 3.24+
QuicUI Tag: v1.0.0-engine-modifications
Related repo: https://github.com/Ikolvi/QuicUICodepush
