+# QuicUI SDK Version Detection
+
+## Overview
+
+The QuicUI Flutter SDK fork includes automatic version detection that allows apps to determine at runtime whether they're built with the QuicUI fork or standard Flutter SDK.
+
+This is critical for:
+- **Code Push Plugin**: Detecting if code push functionality is available
+- **Graceful Degradation**: Showing appropriate warnings when built with wrong SDK
+- **Developer Experience**: Clear feedback about SDK compatibility
+
+## How It Works
+
+### 1. Version String Marker
+
+The QuicUI fork modifies `packages/flutter/lib/src/services/flutter_version.dart`:
+
+```dart
+static const String? version = bool.hasEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')
+    ? '${String.fromEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')} • quicui'
+    : null;
+```
+
+**Result:**
+- QuicUI SDK: `"3.27.0 • quicui"`
+- Standard Flutter: `"3.27.0"`
+
+### 2. Detection in Apps
+
+Apps use the `BuildSDKInfo` class from the code push plugin:
+
+```dart
+import 'package:quicui_code_push_client/src/constants/build_sdk_info.dart';
+
+void main() {
+  if (BuildSDKInfo.isQuicUI) {
+    print('✅ QuicUI Flutter SDK - Code Push enabled');
+  } else {
+    print('⚠️ Standard Flutter SDK - Code Push disabled');
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**Implementation:**
+```dart
+static bool get isQuicUI {
+  final version = flutterVersion ?? '';
+  return version.contains('quicui');
+}
+```
+
+### 3. Build-Time vs Runtime
+
+**Important:** The version string is set at **build time**, not when running `flutter --version`:
+
+```bash
+# This shows the Flutter CLI version (may not include 'quicui')
+$ flutter --version
+Flutter 3.27.0 • channel stable
+
+# But apps built with this SDK will have the marker in FlutterVersion.version
+$ flutter build apk
+# The resulting APK will contain FlutterVersion.version = "3.27.0 • quicui"
+```
+
+## Why This Approach?
+
+### Alternative Approaches Considered
+
+1. **Compile-time constant** (`FlutterVersion.isQuicUIFork`)
+   - ❌ Problem: Causes compilation errors in standard Flutter SDK
+   - ❌ Prevents plugin from being used with both SDKs
+
+2. **Path-based detection** (checking SDK path for 'quicui')
+   - ❌ Problem: Unreliable, users can rename directories
+   - ❌ Doesn't work after app is built/distributed
+
+3. **Dart-define flags** (`--dart-define=IS_QUICUI=true`)
+   - ❌ Problem: Requires manual build configuration
+   - ❌ Easy to forget or misconfigure
+
+4. **Version string check** (CHOSEN ✅)
+   - ✅ Works at both edit time and runtime
+   - ✅ No compilation errors with standard SDK
+   - ✅ Automatic, no manual configuration
+   - ✅ Reliable across builds and distributions
+   - ✅ Plugin can support both SDKs seamlessly
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### Files Modified
+
+1. **packages/flutter/lib/src/services/flutter_version.dart**
+   ```dart
+   // Added ' • quicui' suffix to version string
+   static const String? version = bool.hasEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')
+       ? '${String.fromEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')} • quicui'
+       : null;
+   
+   // Added QuicUI marker constant
+   static const String? quicuiMarker = 'quicui';
+   
+   // Added fork identification flag
+   static const bool isQuicUIFork = true;
+   ```
+
+2. **.quicui_marker** (root directory)
+   ```
+   quicui-fork-v1.0.0
+   ```
+   File-based marker for scripts/tools to detect the fork.
+
+3. **packages/flutter/lib/src/quicui_sdk_marker.dart**
+   ```dart
+   // QuicUI SDK marker file
+   const String quicuiFlutterVersion = '3.38.0-1.0.pre-350';
+   const bool isQuicUIFork = true;
+   ```
+
+### Code Push Plugin Detection
+
+**packages/quicui_code_push_client/lib/src/constants/build_sdk_info.dart:**
+
+```dart
+class BuildSDKInfo {
+  /// Check if running on QuicUI fork by examining version string
+  static bool get isQuicUI {
+    final version = flutterVersion ?? '';
+    return version.contains('quicui');
+  }
+  
+  /// Get the Flutter version string from Platform
+  static String? get flutterVersion {
+    try {
+      final version = FlutterVersion.version;
+      return version;
+    } catch (e) {
+      return null;
+    }
+  }
+  
+  /// Get detailed SDK information for debugging
+  static String getDetailedInfo() {
+    return '''
+SDK Detection Info:
+  Type: ${isQuicUI ? 'QUICUI' : 'FLUTTER'}
+  Is QuicUI Fork: $isQuicUI
+  Flutter Version: ${flutterVersion ?? 'unknown'}
+  QuicUI Marker: ${isQuicUI ? '✓ Present' : '✗ Missing'}
+''';
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Testing SDK Detection
+
+### Test with QuicUI SDK
+
+```bash
+# Build with QuicUI fork
+cd /path/to/quicui-flutter-fork
+export PATH="$(pwd)/bin:$PATH"
+
+cd /path/to/test_app
+flutter build apk --release
+
+# Install and run
+adb install build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk
+adb logcat | grep "SDK"
+
+# Expected output:
+# ✅ QuicUI Flutter SDK detected - Code Push enabled
+```
+
+### Test with Standard Flutter
+
+```bash
+# Build with standard Flutter
+flutter clean
+flutter build apk --release
+
+# Install and run
+adb install build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-release.apk
+adb logcat | grep "SDK"
+
+# Expected output:
+# ⚠️ Standard Flutter SDK detected - QuicUI SDK required
+```
+
+## Cherry-Pick Requirements
+
+When applying QuicUI patches to a new Flutter version, you MUST include these version detection changes:
+
+```bash
+git cherry-pick quicui-v1.0.0-engine
+```
+
+This tag includes:
+- Engine code push files (codepush_loader.h/cc)
+- Android platform files (QuicUICodePushLoader.java, FlutterLoader.java)
+- **SDK version marker** (flutter_version.dart, .quicui_marker)
+
+**Without the version marker changes, SDK detection will fail!**
+
+### Verification
+
+After cherry-picking, verify the marker is present:
+
+```bash
+./.quicui/verify_quicui_patch.sh
+```
+
+Or manually check:
+
+```bash
+# Check version string modification
+grep "quicui" packages/flutter/lib/src/services/flutter_version.dart
+
+# Should output:
+#   ? '${String.fromEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')} • quicui'
+#   static const String? quicuiMarker = 'quicui';
+#   static const bool isQuicUIFork = true;
+```
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### App shows "Standard Flutter SDK" when built with QuicUI fork
+
+**Cause:** Version marker not applied in flutter_version.dart
+
+**Solution:**
+```bash
+cd /path/to/flutter-sdk
+git diff packages/flutter/lib/src/services/flutter_version.dart
+
+# Should show:
+# +    ? '${String.fromEnvironment('FLUTTER_VERSION')} • quicui'
+```
+
+### Plugin won't compile with standard Flutter
+
+**Cause:** Code trying to access `FlutterVersion.isQuicUIFork` directly
+
+**Solution:** Always use version string check:
+```dart
+// ❌ Wrong - causes compilation error
+if (FlutterVersion.isQuicUIFork) { ... }
+
+// ✅ Correct - works with both SDKs
+if (BuildSDKInfo.isQuicUI) { ... }
+```
+
+### Version string doesn't show 'quicui' in `flutter --version`
+
+**This is normal!** The marker appears in the **built app**, not in the CLI output.
+
+To verify:
+```dart
+// In your app
+print(FlutterVersion.version);
+// Should print: "3.27.0 • quicui"
+```
+
+## Summary
+
+The QuicUI SDK version detection:
+1. ✅ Modifies FlutterVersion.version to include ' • quicui' suffix
+2. ✅ Allows runtime detection via simple string check
+3. ✅ Works with both SDKs without compilation errors
+4. ✅ Automatic, no manual configuration needed
+5. ✅ Included in cherry-pick tag `quicui-v1.0.0-engine`
+
+**Key Point:** When migrating to new Flutter versions, cherry-pick the ENTIRE tag to get both engine patches AND version detection.
